// ============================================================================
// DVSM / EIL RUST REPOSITORY — FILE-BY-FILE PURPOSE README
// Author: Daniel J. Dillberg
// ============================================================================
//
// PURPOSE:
// This document explains each major Rust file in the DVSM system,
// describing BOTH:
//
//   1. Unique purpose (what distinguishes the file)
//   2. Broad role (how it fits DVSM overall)
//
// CORE UNIFICATION:
//
// All files are variations of:
//
//   w_{t+1} = T(w_t, σ_t)
//
// with strict separation:
//
//   T = dynamics (state evolution)
//   O = observation (projection only)
//   L = evaluation (loss only)
//   C = constraint deformation (geometry only)
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 dvsm_contraction_kernel.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Defines the minimal stochastic contraction operator.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   This is the mathematical core of the entire system.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Implements contraction update rule
//   - Defines η-stability behavior
//   - Provides abstract state evolution primitive
//
// WHAT IT DOES NOT DO:
//   - No memory
//   - No system structure
//   - No application logic
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is the “atomic equation” everything else wraps or constrains.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 dvsm_bounded_state_machine.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Adds bounded execution semantics to DVSM kernel.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Turns abstract contraction into a safe runtime system.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Enforces bounded scalar state space
//   - Applies stability constraints (η ∈ (0,1))
//   - Adds execution guards (ghost invariants)
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Focuses on *single-state evolution*
//   - No temporal memory (no history buffer)
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is DVSM as a minimal safe “machine” rather than equation.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 dvsm_bounded_fifo_dynamical_system.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Extends DVSM with explicit temporal memory (FIFO window).
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Introduces history-aware contraction dynamics.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Stores state history (VecDeque buffer)
//   - Enables rolling statistics (variance, trend signals)
//   - Introduces temporal smoothing behavior
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Adds memory dimension to system
//   - State is now a *trajectory window*, not a point
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   Represents DVSM with finite horizon temporal structure.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 inverse_adaptive_filter.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Implements DVSM as an adaptive signal cancellation system.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Applies contraction dynamics to real-world signal correction.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Error-driven feedback loop
//   - Adaptive inverse filtering (ANC-style behavior)
//   - Noise cancellation / signal reconstruction
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Explicit feedback correction loop
//   - Uses DVSM as estimator, not just dynamical system
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is the closest file to real DSP / engineering application.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 compression_rust_intro.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Provides interpretive mapping of DVSM contraction to compression.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Explains DVSM as a lossy information compression process.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Reframes contraction as information reduction
//   - Documents performance intuition
//   - Connects DVSM to encoding/representation collapse
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - No new dynamics introduced
//   - Pure conceptual + performance framing layer
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is a semantic bridge file (math → intuition)
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 stochastic_control_loop.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Implements DVSM as a repeated stochastic decision loop.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Wraps contraction kernel into iterative control system.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Repeated sampling of σ_t
//   - Iterative state updates
//   - Feedback-driven execution cycles
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Explicit looped control logic
//   - System-level temporal orchestration
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   Converts DVSM from step function → control process.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 StochasticContractionSystem.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Canonical system-level abstraction of DVSM.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Provides unified system wrapper around kernel + execution logic.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Encapsulates contraction kernel
//   - Manages runtime state lifecycle
//   - Standardizes system execution interface
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Highest-level “clean system API”
//   - Abstracts away internal implementation details
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is the reference implementation of DVSM system design.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 Shared_State.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Enables controlled coupling between multiple DVSM systems.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Introduces shared memory / cross-system interaction layer.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Shared state containers
//   - Cross-system synchronization
//   - Inter-system data visibility
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Breaks isolation between independent systems (carefully)
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is the only explicit coupling mechanism in repository.
//
// WARNING:
//   If misused, it can reintroduce hidden feedback loops.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 Variable_State_v1_v2.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Tracks evolution of state interpretation over time.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Separates state dynamics from semantic meaning changes.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Versioned state metadata
//   - Interpretation refinement layers
//   - Schema evolution (v1 → v2 etc.)
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Does NOT change system dynamics
//   - Only changes meaning of state representation
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   Enables long-term evolution of system interpretation without rewriting kernel.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 EIL_Hardended.rs
// ============================================================================
//
// UNIQUE PURPOSE:
//   Enforces strict structural invariants across DVSM system.
//
// BROAD ROLE:
//   Acts as global constraint enforcement and system hardening layer.
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
//   - Enforces T/O/L separation discipline
//   - Prevents illegal cross-layer coupling
//   - Applies formal reduction rules
//   - Validates structural integrity of systems
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DISTINCT:
//   - Not tied to any single DVSM layer
//   - Applies system-wide enforcement rules
//
// SIGNIFICANCE:
//   This is the “safety kernel” of the entire architecture.
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧭 GLOBAL SYSTEM SUMMARY
// ============================================================================
//
// Across all files, the DVSM repository is:
//
//   NOT a collection of independent systems
//   NOT multiple models
//   NOT separate frameworks
//
// It is:
//
//   a stratified implementation of a single stochastic contraction operator
//
// Each file is a controlled transformation of:
//
//   - dynamics (T)
//   - observation (O)
//   - evaluation (L)
//   - constraint geometry (C)
//
// across different structural layers:
//
//   Kernel → Machine → Memory → Control → Coupling → Interpretation → Hardening
//
// ============================================================================
// 🧠 FINAL INVARIANT
// ============================================================================
//
// No file introduces new fundamental dynamics.
//
// Each file only:
//
//   - constrains behavior
//   - adds structure
//   - introduces memory or coupling
//   - or enforces invariants
//
// All reduce back to:
//
//       w_{t+1} = T(w_t, σ_t)
//
// ============================================================================
// ============================================================================
// DVSM / SYSTEMS REPOSITORY — ARCHITECTURE README (v1.0)
// STRICT DETERMINISM + CONSTRAINT-BASED CONTROL STACK
// ============================================================================
